# C11.1: a class on the *user's* classpath is importable, under both backends.
#
# `Hello` lives in a jar built from `Hello.java` and nowhere else, so this probe can only pass
# when that jar is reachable. `run.py` launches it as `java -cp "oq.jar:fixture.jar"` rather
# than `java -jar`; `-jar` ignores both `CLASSPATH` and the working directory, which is why the
# gap this closes was real. The jar is built on every run from committed source rather than kept
# in the tree: a committed jar is invisible to review. A missing `javac` is a failure, never a
# skip, because the harness already needs a JDK to build probes.
#
# The class is deliberately not on the CLI jar's own classpath and not in the default package
# of anything this build produces, so a pass cannot be an accident of `oq.jar` already
# containing a `Hello`.
use Hello
print Hello.greet()
